+/// The receive window we advertise, in bytes, and the most we hold of
+/// segments that came ahead of a gap. Advertising all of `u16::MAX << 8`
+/// let the peer put 16 MiB in flight through the tunnel, and with every
+/// segment after a lost one dropped, it had to send them all again
+/// (Atelier, 10 Nov 2026).
+const RECV_WINDOW: u32 = 1 << 20; // 1 MiB
+
 /// Default cap on bytes in flight per connection, in bytes. Overridden via
 /// [`Adapter::set_send_window`].
 const DEFAULT_SEND_WINDOW: usize = 1 << 20; // 1 MiB
